WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.703
[mysterious music]

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.204
 Alex, Trevor,
congratulations, you

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.673
boys are now in the
third and final round

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.142
of this competition.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.843
And now it's time to send
you back to your home forges

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:15.415
to recreate this iconic weapon--

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.017
J. Neilson's war scythe.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.185
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.386
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.721
 Yes, sir.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.724 line:7%
[rock music]

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.125
ALEX: I'm back in my home forge.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.693
I got all my own tools.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.997
But I am certainly going to
miss having a power hammer.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:32.465
I've got to do all this by hand.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.534
It's going to be a
much bigger challenge.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:39.772
Today, I am rough forging the
scythe portion of the weapon.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.274
There's just a lot of material.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.242
And I'm doing all this
with a hand hammer.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.678
So it's just going
to take a while.

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:49.481
So as I'm drying out my billet,
my hammer just breaks on me.

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:52.418
I had to switch to a
different hammer mid-hear.

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:56.389
So just one other thing
I got to deal with.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.995
 At the start of day 2,
I'm going to work on forging

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:05.097
out another scythe head.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.500
I'm going to use my first
blade as a template,

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.068
hopefully get everything
cleaned up so I can

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:12.005
heat treat by this afternoon.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.507
Now, the storm is starting
to come back through.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:18.511
I'm hoping we don't
have a problem.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.213
Oh, the power went out.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.215
I'm really not going to be able
to use my mill or my grinder.

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.950
Without these power
tools, I'm not going

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.752
to be able to finish my blade.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.321
This is not what I want.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.323 line:7%
ALEX: It's the start to day 2.

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:33.793 line:0%
So I decided to make the bottom
blade out of 1095 so it doesn't

00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:35.762 line:7%
need to be terribly flexible.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.197
Everything seems
to be going well.

00:01:38.263 --> 00:01:39.531
So I'm about to start grinding.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.835
And I go to check my
blade, and the main blade

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.336
is under 12 inches.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:48.107
I'm almost a quarter of
an inch under parameters.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.043
Luckily, I haven't
started grinding yet,

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.479
so I can still go back and
forge the extra bit out.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.749
So I'm really glad I found this
problem before it was too late.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.818
[whirring]

00:01:58.884 --> 00:02:00.086
Finished all the rough grinding.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:01.654
Now, I want to get the quench.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.894
Heat treat went well.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.262
I'm really glad day 2 is done.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.730
I feel like I got
a lot accomplished.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.267 line:0%
So I'm definitely feeling
a lot better today.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.736 line:7%
TREVOR: The power came back on.

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:18.371
But right now, I just want
to get that smaller blade

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.406
heat treated and work
on the bigger blade,

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:21.875
and then get into
making the handle.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.648
Everything looks
pretty straight.

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.517
The next step right now is going
to be heat treating the forks.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:34.520
And then, I'll finish everything
up and make it look real nice.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.191
[rock music]

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.559
The forks heat treated great.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.462
I'm going to use this
aluminum bat to test it.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.665
If the aluminum bat
damages these forks any,

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:46.533
it's a problem.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.171
That's pristine.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.540
I have to work on
this wood handle now.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.241
Everything is
fitting really well.

00:02:56.308 --> 00:02:57.810
I'm going to move on
to the detail work.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:00.713
[howling]

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.482 line:0%
ALEX: So it's the
morning of day 4.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.285
Right now, all I got to
do is the final assembly.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.922
I'm in the homestretch.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.558
It feels very tight.

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:15.928
So judges, we're looking forward
to you swinging this blade.

00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:17.129
It's going to be a beast.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:20.166
And I hope it handles well.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.634
Oh, jeez.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:25.537
[spooky music]

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:27.540
 Trevor, Alex, welcome
back to the forge.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.975
You boys have had four
days at your home forges

00:03:30.075 --> 00:03:31.510
to work on your war scythes.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.946
Your blades will now be
subjected to three tests.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:37.950
There will be a strength test,
a sharpness test, but up first,

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:45.491
our very own dealer of death,
the doer of deadly deeds,

00:03:45.557 --> 00:03:49.662
the kill test master,
Doug Marcaida.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.064
[evil laughter]

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:54.634
 Yeah, he just looks
like a murderer.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:55.868
I am really nervous.

00:04:00.105 --> 00:04:03.643
[rock music]

00:04:24.963 --> 00:04:26.199
 All right, Alex.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.901
The balance is light,
allowing it to be a very

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:30.235
fast weapon that you can use.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:33.372
It will handle long-handed
or for close quarters.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:35.642
Your weapon will kill.

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.579
All right, Trevor,
trick-or-treat?

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:41.180
 Treat.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.348
 Indeed.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.048
It will be a treat.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:46.052
[rock music]

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:18.317
All right, Trevor, the tip alone
penetrates deeply into the gut,

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.052
and the edges here
are sharp enough to,

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.120
well, make him lose his head.

00:05:22.187 --> 00:05:24.223
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:24.991
 Thank you, sir.

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.464
 All right, smiths, welcome
to the strength test,

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.033
the dreaded coffin challenge.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.534
[thunder]

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.470
I'm gonna take these bones
and beat them repeatedly

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.305
into the blade of your scythes.

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.741
And Alex, you're locked
in and ready to go first.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:43.609
You're ready?

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:44.543
 Yep.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.745
 That's what I want to hear.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:46.746
 [laughs]

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:50.116
[suspenseful music]

00:05:57.156 --> 00:06:00.058
[rock music]

00:06:00.125 --> 00:06:03.629
[grunts]

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:11.737
 Alex, you survived.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:13.105
Good job.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.173
The only issue I have, you have
some slight rolling on the edge

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.243
and the head of this moves.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.111
So it's not secure anymore.

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:20.279
But your edge held up great.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.179
Good job.

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:22.348
 Thank you.

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:24.216
 How you feeling, Trevor?

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:25.451
- Pretty good right now.
- Good.

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:26.519
Well, we'll see you
feel in a minute.

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:29.655
[suspenseful music]

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.593
[rock music]

00:06:46.104 --> 00:06:46.839
Nice job, Trevor.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.174
It held up well.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.442
Your edge is still
good, nice and sharp.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.111
Everything's still tight.

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:53.245
Good job.

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:54.414
 Thank you.

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.887
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the sharpness

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:02.688
test, the zombie surprise.

00:07:05.857 --> 00:07:08.760
To test the edge of your weapon,
I going to take your scythe

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:12.097
and cut through this rope,
thereby releasing the surprise.

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:13.499
 All right.

00:07:13.599 --> 00:07:14.367
 Alex, you're up first.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:15.801
You ready?

00:07:15.901 --> 00:07:16.969
 Certainly.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.945
[rock music]

00:07:42.427 --> 00:07:43.930
 (WHISPERS) Shit.

00:07:47.366 --> 00:07:50.068
 All right, Alex it
cut easily on the rope.

00:07:50.135 --> 00:07:54.907
When you're puncturing this,
it cuts through and slices.

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:56.408
It will cut.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:57.710
 Thank you.

00:07:57.776 --> 00:07:58.877
 All right, Trevor, your turn.

00:07:58.978 --> 00:07:59.978
So you ready?

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.314
 Oh, yeah.

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:04.484
[suspenseful music]

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:08.488
[thunder]

00:08:11.356 --> 00:08:15.261
[rock music]

00:08:38.584 --> 00:08:39.785
 All right, Trevor.

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:41.720
The edge that you
have here lends itself

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:43.622
to cut the rope much easier.

00:08:43.689 --> 00:08:45.257
When you're
puncturing, it starts

00:08:45.357 --> 00:08:46.692
to cut all the way through.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.894
Overall, sir, it will cut.

00:08:48.994 --> 00:08:49.662
 Thank you.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:55.133
 All right, bladesmiths, you
guys have done fantastic work.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.803
But only one of you can be
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:57.903 --> 00:09:02.908
And that champion is Trevor.

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:06.578
Congratulations, you are the
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:09.415
Alex, unfortunately, your
blade took some damage

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:10.516
in our strength test.

00:09:10.582 --> 00:09:12.084
You did great work, my friend.

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:15.987
But at this time, I have to ask
you to please exit the forge.

00:09:16.054 --> 00:09:18.057
 Ultimately, it came
down to the construction.

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.526
Unfortunately, mine just
came a little bit loose.

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:22.061
And that was enough.

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:27.532
One of my main goals was that
I wanted to go the whole way.

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:28.600
I certainly did that.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.369
I'm very proud of myself.

00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:31.603
I think I definitely
made a blade

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:33.205
that can intimidate anyone.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:37.476
 Well, Trevor, the
judges all agree,

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.478
you made a damn near
perfect war scythe,

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:41.380
which has earned you the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:43.548
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:09:43.648 --> 00:09:44.683
Good job, brother.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.086
Come on forward and
shake our hands.

00:09:47.153 --> 00:09:48.921
TREVOR: I won!

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:50.255
Woo!

00:09:50.355 --> 00:09:52.391
I think the biggest thing I
learned was to keep on trying.

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:55.227
If something doesn't go your
way, don't get upset about it,

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.462
just keep moving forward.

00:09:57.529 --> 00:09:59.464
This was a perfect
Halloween experience.

00:09:59.531 --> 00:10:00.766
I feel like I just
went trick-or-treating

00:10:00.866 --> 00:10:03.535
and I got a pillowcase
full of candy.

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.671
[rock music]

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.005
[evil laughter]

00:10:07.072 --> 00:10:08.072
[screaming]

